[32m+[m[32m### Deep Observability Plugin[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mThe `openclaw-deep-observability-plugin` provides richer, hierarchical OTLP[m
[32m+[m[32mtraces compared to the built-in `diagnostics-otel` plugin. It emits[m
[32m+[m[32mparent-child span trees with per-tool timing, LLM call isolation, and[m
[32m+[m[32msession lifecycle spans.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mThe plugin works for **root agents** and **peer agents** (independent[m
[32m+[m[32mOpenClaw sessions) — which is how Mycelium's agents are structured. It[m
[32m+[m[32mdoes **not** emit traces for internal sub-agent calls within a single[m
[32m+[m[32mOpenClaw session.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m#### Setup[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m```bash[m
[32m+[m[32mmycelium adapter add openclaw --step=otel --step=deep-observability[m
[32m+[m[32m```[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mBoth steps should be run together. `--step=otel` configures the built-in[m
[32m+[m[32m`diagnostics-otel` plugin which emits the flat counters and histograms[m
[32m+[m[32mthat power `mycelium metrics show`. `--step=deep-observability` adds the[m
[32m+[m[32mhierarchical trace spans stored in `traces.db`. Without `--step=otel`,[m
[32m+[m[32mthe OpenClaw panels in `mycelium metrics show` will have no data.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mThe `--step=deep-observability` portion:[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m1. Installs the plugin from ClawhHub (`openclaw plugins install`)[m
[32m+[m[32m2. Adds the plugin to `plugins.allow` and `plugins.entries` in[m
[32m+[m[32m   `~/.openclaw/openclaw.json` with the OTLP endpoint matching the[m
[32m+[m[32m   collector port[m
[32m+[m[32m3. Patches model cost and `compat.supportsUsageInStreaming` settings[m
[32m+[m[32m4. Restarts the OpenClaw gateway to pick up the config[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mThe resulting `openclaw.json` plugin entry looks like:[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m```json[m
[32m+[m[32m{[m
[32m+[m[32m  "plugins": {[m
[32m+[m[32m    "allow": ["openclaw-deep-observability-plugin"],[m
[32m+[m[32m    "entries": {[m
[32m+[m[32m      "openclaw-deep-observability-plugin": {[m
[32m+[m[32m        "enabled": true,[m
[32m+[m[32m        "config": {[m
[32m+[m[32m          "endpoint": "http://localhost:4318",[m
[32m+[m[32m          "protocol": "http/protobuf",[m
[32m+[m[32m          "traces": true,[m
[32m+[m[32m          "metrics": true,[m
[32m+[m[32m          "logs": false,[m
[32m+[m[32m          "captureContent": false,[m
[32m+[m[32m          "metricsIntervalMs": 5000[m
[32m+[m[32m        }[m
[32m+[m[32m      }[m
[32m+[m[32m    }[m
[32m+[m[32m  }[m
[32m+[m[32m}[m
[32m+[m[32m```[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mWhen running OpenClaw in a Docker container, the endpoint is automatically[m
[32m+[m[32mset to `http://host.docker.internal:4318`.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mThe deep observability plugin and the built-in `diagnostics-otel` plugin[m
[32m+[m[32mcan run side by side. Both emit to the same collector. The deep plugin's[m
[32m+[m[32mtraces are richer (hierarchical spans) while `diagnostics-otel` provides[m
[32m+[m[32mthe flat counter/histogram metrics used by `mycelium metrics show`.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m### Trace Storage (TraceStore)[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mRaw OTLP trace spans are persisted to `~/.mycelium/traces.db` (SQLite,[m
[32m+[m[32mWAL mode) by the `TraceStore` class in `collector.py`. This runs in[m
[32m+[m[32mparallel with the `MetricsStore` — on every `/v1/traces` POST, the[m
[32m+[m[32mcollector feeds bytes to both stores.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m**Schema:**[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m| Column           | Type  | Description                                     |[m
[32m+[m[32m| ---------------- | ----- | ----------------------------------------------- |[m
[32m+[m[32m| `trace_id`       | TEXT  | Hex trace ID                                    |[m
[32m+[m[32m| `span_id`        | TEXT  | Hex span ID (primary key)                       |[m
[32m+[m[32m| `parent_span_id` | TEXT  | Parent span ID (empty for root spans)           |[m
[32m+[m[32m| `name`           | TEXT  | Span operation name                             |[m
[32m+[m[32m| `kind`           | TEXT  | `internal`, `server`, `client`, `producer`, `consumer` |[m
[32m+[m[32m| `service`        | TEXT  | `service.name` from the OTLP resource           |[m
[32m+[m[32m| `start_time`     | TEXT  | ISO 8601 timestamp                              |[m
[32m+[m[32m| `duration_ms`    | REAL  | Span duration in milliseconds                   |[m
[32m+[m[32m| `status`         | TEXT  | `unset`, `ok`, or `error`                       |[m
[32m+[m[32m| `status_message` | TEXT  | Error message when status is `error`            |[m
[32m+[m[32m| `attributes`     | TEXT  | JSON-encoded span attributes                    |[m
[32m+[m[32m| `created_at`     | TEXT  | Insertion timestamp (used for retention cleanup) |[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m**Retention:** Spans older than 7 days are deleted automatically[m
[32m+[m[32m(checked hourly and at collector shutdown). The cleanup runs[m
[32m+[m[32m`PRAGMA incremental_vacuum` to reclaim disk space.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m**API access:** The FastAPI backend exposes `GET /api/observability/traces/recent?limit=100`[m
[32m+[m[32mwhich reads `traces.db` directly and returns trace summaries with full span[m
[32m+[m[32mtrees for waterfall rendering. Each trace includes `root_span`, `agent`,[m
[32m+[m[32m`duration_ms`, `span_count`, `has_error`, and the full `spans` array.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mThe backend also exposes `GET /api/observability/collector` which returns the[m
[32m+[m[32mcollector-written `metrics.json` contents (counters, histograms, sessions,[m
[32m+[m[32mscrape) — excluding the `backend` key that duplicates `GET /api/observability`.[m
[32m+[m
